<title>UK: Lloyd's issues results of seventh capacity auction.</title>
<headline>Lloyd's issues results of seventh capacity auction.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lloyd's of London on Friday issued the result of the seventh auction of syndicate capacity for the 1997 underwriting year.</p>
<p>In the auction, held between 30 September and 3 October, a total of 82 million stg of market capacity was auctioned realising a total value of 3.5 million stg.</p>
<p>Subscription orders (offers to buy) entered during the seventh auction  totalled 327 million stg while tenders (offers to sell) totalled 102 million stg.  </p>
<p>Cumulatively, the seven auctions held this year have resulted in 1.351 billion stg of capacity (representing 13 percent of 1996 underwriting capacity) being auctioned successfully, realising 30.7 million stg in respect of 124 Lloyd's syndicates.</p>
<p>The eighth and final 1996 auction will be held between 14-17 October.</p>
